## Decision 12 - Cold Service Cache And Singleton Purge

Problem: Several Tick-transitive SHINOBU methods still resolved services through `GlobalRegistry.*` or `ObjectPoolManager.Instance`: DataVault slice resolution, JobAdmission scheduling, MacroDB eviction, AssetLifecycle release drain, ObjectPool hydration/prewarm/despawn, VRAM monitor reads, AmbientBiota threat checks, and async persistence refresh.
Solution: Added cold cached service fields populated by `RefreshColdServiceCache()` from Awake/TryRegister. Runtime streaming methods now use cached `_dataVault`, `_jobAdmissionService`, `_macroDatabaseService`, `_assetLifecycleGovernor`, `_vramMonitor`, `_objectPoolManager`, `_ambientBiotaService`, and `_asyncPersistenceService`. Removed the `ObjectPoolManager.Instance` fallback; if Boot did not register the pool in `GlobalRegistry`, hydration/prewarm fails closed.
Rejected Alternatives: per-frame service-locator reads, classic singleton fallback, and hot-path retry of `SaveRuntime` discovery.
Scalability potential: Low tier avoids service-locator churn under storage pressure; Middle/High/Ultra keep the same decoupled seams while expanding residency budgets.
Hardware Impact: removes hot-path dependency lookup and branch clutter; measured microseconds remain unavailable until profiler proof.

